The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (ifmgd->auth_data) {
    // Authentication process running
}
```
Reason:
The condition checks if there is an ongoing authentication process. If the system is suspended while this process is still running, it does not get aborted because cfg80211 does not track it, leading to potential issues such as errors in firmware.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ieee80211_send_deauth_disassoc(sdata, ifmgd->auth_data->bss->bssid, IEEE80211_STYPE_DEAUTH, WLAN_REASON_DEAUTH_LEAVING, false, frame_buf);
ieee80211_destroy_auth_data(sdata, false);
```
Reason:
These statements ensure that if an authentication attempt is ongoing at the time of suspension, it is explicitly aborted by sending a deauthentication frame and cleaning up the authentication data, hence resolving the race condition between suspension and authentication attempts.

